1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,004
With the dangerous condition
your heart is in,

2
00:00:04,971 --> 00:00:06,406
I couldn't just ignore you.

3
00:00:06,473 --> 00:00:07,540
It's none of your business.

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,281
Hey!

5
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:20,286
FREELANCE SURGEON
MICHIKO DAIMON

6
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:23,790
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

7
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:27,727
Your cyanosis isn't improving.

8
00:00:29,162 --> 00:00:31,131
There's nothing I can do for you.

9
00:00:32,465 --> 00:00:36,302
Doctor, I am a physician as well.

10
00:00:36,569 --> 00:00:37,971
I know...

11
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,472
ASSISTANT HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
NICHOLAS TANGE

12
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:42,308
...what's happening inside my body.

13
00:00:44,844 --> 00:00:46,479
Just give me sedatives.

14
00:00:47,847 --> 00:00:50,083
That's all I need.

15
00:00:55,688 --> 00:01:00,260
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

16
00:01:02,862 --> 00:01:05,165
You took a plea bargain?

17
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:09,002
Everything was done by
Nicholas Tange alone.

18
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:11,237
I wasn't involved at all.

19
00:01:11,704 --> 00:01:14,841
I'm sure you've heard
the term "unscrupulous."

20
00:01:15,508 --> 00:01:19,913
That word describes you perfectly.

21
00:01:19,979 --> 00:01:21,381
CHIEF ADMINISTRATOR
YU SAMEJIMA

22
00:01:23,149 --> 00:01:24,684
If things continue like this,

23
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:27,987
Totei University Hospital could
fall into bankruptcy.

24
00:01:28,855 --> 00:01:29,889
Bankruptcy?

25
00:01:30,323 --> 00:01:32,492
Why don't we work together,
Director Hiruma?

26
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:35,028
What do you mean by that?

27
00:01:35,128 --> 00:01:39,232
We'll start a new fund and get investors.

28
00:01:39,566 --> 00:01:42,469
We'll call it the Hiruma Fund.

29
00:01:43,069 --> 00:01:45,105
Naturally, included in this
investment plan is

30
00:01:45,238 --> 00:01:48,741
the 30-billion investment
created for Totei University Hospital

31
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:51,945
by former Assistant Director Tange.

32
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,850
But you know, Samejima,

33
00:01:58,084 --> 00:02:01,488
I can find absolutely no reason at all

34
00:02:02,322 --> 00:02:04,924
why I should trust you.

35
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:08,061
Who is Totei University for?

36
00:02:09,596 --> 00:02:10,730
Director Hiruma,

37
00:02:11,531 --> 00:02:16,202
Totei University was made for you.
Isn't that right?

38
00:02:23,076 --> 00:02:24,611
That's not a bad reason.

39
00:02:27,947 --> 00:02:29,582
Go ahead with the plan.

40
00:02:30,884 --> 00:02:32,085
Yes, sir.

41
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:37,090
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

42
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:40,527
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

43
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:44,597
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

44
00:02:46,032 --> 00:02:50,637
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance maverick doctor,
who was never part of</i>

45
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:54,440
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

46
00:02:56,676 --> 00:03:00,213
There's a three-centimeter tumor
on the apex of the right lung.

47
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,949
It's a schwannoma on the brachial plexus,

48
00:03:03,149 --> 00:03:04,150
no doubt about it.

49
00:03:05,151 --> 00:03:06,953
This is going to be rough.

50
00:03:14,561 --> 00:03:16,396
DADDY

51
00:03:25,838 --> 00:03:27,006
Dr. Ebina!

52
00:03:29,008 --> 00:03:30,376
What's the matter?

53
00:03:33,179 --> 00:03:34,214
You know,

54
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:39,552
I was wondering if life insurance
will pay in the case of suicide.

55
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,321
Suicide?

56
00:03:42,622 --> 00:03:44,157
Are you crazy?

57
00:03:44,324 --> 00:03:47,994
You know my daughter, Aya, right?

58
00:03:48,795 --> 00:03:50,830
Yes, she looks just like you.

59
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:53,233
We may look alike, but unlike me,

60
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,569
she's talented and intelligent.

61
00:03:59,172 --> 00:04:00,907
She wants to go to medical school.

62
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,408
That's great!

63
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:05,979
But medical school costs money,

64
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,915
and I've become a plebe now.

65
00:04:10,283 --> 00:04:14,387
Is that what this is about?
You're worried about money?

66
00:04:14,887 --> 00:04:16,122
I can get a part-time job.

67
00:04:16,856 --> 00:04:18,157
I don't have time.

68
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:19,626
You don't?

69
00:04:21,327 --> 00:04:22,528
I've

70
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:25,765
got cancer.

71
00:04:29,836 --> 00:04:31,604
You're kidding!

72
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:35,408
Wait! No running!

73
00:04:36,843 --> 00:04:39,912
I'm don't want the operation.

74
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:42,148
Why not?

75
00:04:43,049 --> 00:04:46,219
If I get the operation,
I won't be able to play the piano.

76
00:04:47,353 --> 00:04:48,888
Who told you that?

77
00:04:50,757 --> 00:04:52,091
Five different doctors.

78
00:04:52,859 --> 00:04:56,362
All the doctors who ran my tests said so.

79
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:01,200
Don't believe what those guys said.

80
00:05:02,068 --> 00:05:05,705
Will I be able to play the piano again?

81
00:05:05,805 --> 00:05:06,806
I swear it.

82
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:09,075
After my operation, you will.

83
00:05:11,244 --> 00:05:13,313
If you leave it to Dr. Daimon,
you'll be fine.

84
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:16,949
Dr. Daimon's forte is surgery.

85
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:19,319
Great!

86
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:21,954
The only thing I'm good at is
the playing piano.

87
00:05:22,789 --> 00:05:26,459
I'm terrible at math and Japanese.
I'm terrible at PE too.

88
00:05:26,726 --> 00:05:28,394
That's going too far.

89
00:05:28,461 --> 00:05:31,564
Me too. The only thing
I'm good at is surgery.

90
00:05:31,631 --> 00:05:32,799
That's exactly right.

91
00:05:32,899 --> 00:05:33,900
That hurts.

92
00:05:34,967 --> 00:05:38,004
But thanks to Nicholas' help,

93
00:05:38,571 --> 00:05:40,239
I play piano as good as anyone.

94
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:43,109
"Nicholas"? What do you mean by that?

95
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:46,479
Thanks to the money Nicholas gave me,

96
00:05:46,779 --> 00:05:48,981
I was able to go to the Juilliard School.

97
00:05:49,649 --> 00:05:50,750
Not just me either.

98
00:05:51,384 --> 00:05:55,221
Nicholas is an amazing person
who help lots of kids.

99
00:05:56,622 --> 00:05:57,790
Is that right?

100
00:05:59,559 --> 00:06:02,662
Will I really be cured?

101
00:06:04,764 --> 00:06:05,998
Don't worry.

102
00:06:07,467 --> 00:06:10,203
I never fail.

103
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:15,875
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

104
00:06:16,275 --> 00:06:20,446
<i>authority, and restrictions.</i>

105
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:23,883
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

106
00:06:24,283 --> 00:06:25,918
<i>are her weapons.</i>

107
00:06:37,263 --> 00:06:39,031
- Run the stimulus.
- Got it.

108
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:46,205
Flexing of the little and ring fingers.

109
00:06:46,839 --> 00:06:48,040
That's the ulnar nerve.

110
00:06:48,107 --> 00:06:50,243
C8 is completely engulfed in the tumor.

111
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:52,745
It's worse than expected.
We can't remove it all.

112
00:06:56,582 --> 00:06:57,750
Dr. Daimon?

113
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:03,756
Change of procedures.

114
00:07:03,856 --> 00:07:06,592
We'll detach C8 nerves
and completely remove the tumor.

115
00:07:06,859 --> 00:07:07,860
- Lower my loupe.
- Right.

116
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:11,230
Hold on! He may never play
the piano again if you do that!

117
00:07:11,964 --> 00:07:14,066
What are you waiting for? Get a graft.

118
00:07:14,167 --> 00:07:15,201
- Metzenbaum.
- Here.

119
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:16,702
Prep the lower thigh.

120
00:07:16,969 --> 00:07:18,037
Don't do this!

121
00:07:19,205 --> 00:07:20,239
Dr. Daimon!

122
00:07:31,984 --> 00:07:33,286
What are his vitals?

123
00:07:33,352 --> 00:07:36,923
BP, 112 over 75. Pulse, 80, sinus.

124
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:38,791
Done.

125
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:43,162
Dr. Daimon's surgeries sure are amazing.

126
00:07:48,034 --> 00:07:49,302
Nice work.

127
00:07:49,769 --> 00:07:51,204
Nice work.

128
00:07:57,944 --> 00:08:00,313
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

129
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:03,916
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

130
00:08:18,631 --> 00:08:20,900
Kazuto Yoshiyuki's surgery was a success.

131
00:08:21,467 --> 00:08:23,069
We'll hold a press conference right away.

132
00:08:23,402 --> 00:08:25,638
This will improve your image too,
Director Hiruma.

133
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:29,175
That's not the kind of thing
to say out loud, Ebina.

134
00:08:29,308 --> 00:08:31,344
- Sit down.
- Yes, sir.

135
00:08:35,281 --> 00:08:36,515
- Ebina.
- Yes?

136
00:08:36,582 --> 00:08:38,351
You don't look well.

137
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,119
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.

138
00:08:40,419 --> 00:08:43,122
Actually, there's something

139
00:08:43,956 --> 00:08:46,092
that I want to tell you two.

140
00:08:46,158 --> 00:08:47,159
- Okay.
- Okay.

141
00:08:47,226 --> 00:08:50,129
Me and that Samejima will be

142
00:08:51,631 --> 00:08:53,232
working together.

143
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:55,835
Why are you doing that?

144
00:08:56,669 --> 00:08:58,237
He's a traitor.

145
00:08:58,304 --> 00:09:00,806
He's creating the Hiruma Fund

146
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,476
in order to put Totei University Hospital

147
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:07,113
completely under my control.

148
00:09:08,447 --> 00:09:11,851
Therefore, I want one of you two

149
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:16,622
to be the Assistant Hospital Director.

150
00:09:17,323 --> 00:09:18,424
Assistant Hospital Director?

151
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,562
Try gripping it.

152
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,999
My right fingers won't move.

153
00:09:27,767 --> 00:09:28,801
Try it again.

154
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:34,073
I told you. They don't move.

155
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:36,175
You're a big liar, Dr. Daimon!

156
00:09:39,979 --> 00:09:41,347
Can we talk, Dr. Daimon?

157
00:09:46,552 --> 00:09:48,688
I told you in surgery this would happen!

158
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:50,623
You've clearly made a mistake, Dr. Daimon!

159
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:52,124
A mistake?

160
00:09:52,358 --> 00:09:53,392
By Dr. Daimon?

161
00:09:53,559 --> 00:09:55,461
It was supposed to be
a subcapsular removal,

162
00:09:55,561 --> 00:09:57,530
but you detached his nerves
for a complete removal!

163
00:09:57,797 --> 00:10:00,399
A subcapsular removal wouldn't
have removed the whole tumor.

164
00:10:00,566 --> 00:10:03,903
If the tumor remained, he would relapse.

165
00:10:04,303 --> 00:10:06,539
Then he would never play piano again.

166
00:10:07,073 --> 00:10:09,909
The reality is that Kazuto
can't move his fingers even now.

167
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,645
You said your surgery
would allow him to play piano.

168
00:10:13,646 --> 00:10:16,148
That was a lie to get him
to agree to the surgery, wasn't it?

169
00:10:17,350 --> 00:10:20,620
Dr. Daimon, you've destroyed
his talent and his future.

170
00:10:22,521 --> 00:10:23,623
His future?

171
00:10:23,856 --> 00:10:24,991
What's so funny?

172
00:10:28,227 --> 00:10:30,329
All you're thinking about is the present.

173
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:36,836
SURGEON
KOHEI TAKO

174
00:10:42,241 --> 00:10:44,644
- I'm home.
- Welcome back.

175
00:10:50,883 --> 00:10:51,917
Wait.

176
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:53,886
The cafeteria lady!

177
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:55,621
What are you doing here?

178
00:10:55,788 --> 00:10:58,124
It's been such a long time, Ms. Daimon!

179
00:10:58,190 --> 00:11:00,726
She just returned from a trip
around the world.

180
00:11:00,793 --> 00:11:01,961
A trip around the world?

181
00:11:02,061 --> 00:11:03,629
You're that rich?

182
00:11:09,068 --> 00:11:12,338
Oh, that's right. Michiko,
she brought us lots of souvenirs.

183
00:11:12,438 --> 00:11:15,274
You're right!
Look at all these souvenirs! Amazing!

184
00:11:16,308 --> 00:11:19,278
It is not amazing, you thieving minx!

185
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:21,313
What? Ben Casey!

186
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,716
Don't you be stealing!

187
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:29,588
I heard you're hitting on my
Assistant Hospital Director Tange.

188
00:11:29,655 --> 00:11:31,791
- What?
- That's right.

189
00:11:31,891 --> 00:11:34,260
She's been lying that
she's his common-law wife

190
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,829
and seen him several times
at the detention center.

191
00:11:38,164 --> 00:11:41,167
So can he be cured?

192
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,903
He has a congenital heart disease.

193
00:11:44,236 --> 00:11:47,073
He needs surgery that nobody
has ever performed.

194
00:11:47,306 --> 00:11:49,275
- Oh, dear!
- The biggest problem is

195
00:11:49,642 --> 00:11:52,478
his attitude toward fighting his disease.

196
00:11:52,945 --> 00:11:54,046
His attitude?

197
00:11:54,113 --> 00:11:57,083
Mr. Tange is refusing all treatment.

198
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:59,585
If the patient refuses to live,

199
00:11:59,685 --> 00:12:01,987
the doctor has no way of fighting.

200
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:04,790
All right.

201
00:12:06,158 --> 00:12:09,361
You just take care of the rest. Okay?

202
00:12:20,306 --> 00:12:24,076
Why did you come to see me?

203
00:12:24,176 --> 00:12:27,847
I thought you would be lonely
all by yourself.

204
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:31,984
Have you been well since we last met?

205
00:12:33,686 --> 00:12:35,354
Never mind about me.

206
00:12:36,322 --> 00:12:39,358
You should be worrying about yourself.

207
00:12:44,730 --> 00:12:48,768
Dr. Daimon asked you to come here,
didn't she?

208
00:12:49,902 --> 00:12:52,938
No. I wanted to come.

209
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:57,743
I've been wanting to see you.

210
00:13:01,981 --> 00:13:04,283
Please, get the surgery.

211
00:13:04,717 --> 00:13:07,887
I'm already very old.

212
00:13:09,889 --> 00:13:13,425
I have no reason to live.

213
00:13:13,592 --> 00:13:17,163
I want you to live.

214
00:13:18,731 --> 00:13:20,399
Isn't that reason enough?

215
00:13:33,245 --> 00:13:34,713
- Mr. Tange!
- Hey!

216
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,982
- Are you all right?
- Mr. Tange!

217
00:13:37,082 --> 00:13:39,218
Don't die!

218
00:13:39,351 --> 00:13:41,220
He may need an open-chest cardiac massage.

219
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:43,155
Rush him to the operating room.

220
00:13:51,263 --> 00:13:54,166
His heart's been stopped for 23 minutes.
He's had 20 minutes of CPR.

221
00:13:54,233 --> 00:13:56,635
Pupil diameter, six millimeters.
No light reflex.

222
00:13:57,369 --> 00:13:59,004
- Two milliliters of epinephrine.
- Got it.

223
00:13:59,238 --> 00:14:00,406
- I'll take over.
- Right.

224
00:14:04,043 --> 00:14:05,344
Two hundred joules.

225
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:09,915
Nothing.

226
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:28,601
Thirty minutes since starting CPR.

227
00:14:28,667 --> 00:14:29,802
This is bad.

228
00:14:30,169 --> 00:14:31,604
Lower his temperature.

229
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:34,340
Circulation via PCPS. What temperature?

230
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,841
- Thirty-four.
- Got it.

231
00:14:36,308 --> 00:14:37,877
- Full transfusion.
- Right.

232
00:14:39,311 --> 00:14:40,179
Right.

233
00:14:42,748 --> 00:14:45,885
Nichotan, hurry up and wake up!

234
00:14:46,752 --> 00:14:48,220
You can do it!

235
00:14:49,855 --> 00:14:52,358
This is where you are?
You can't come in here.

236
00:14:52,424 --> 00:14:53,626
Save Mr. Tange!

237
00:14:55,027 --> 00:14:56,195
He'll be alright.

238
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:04,169
- Excuse me. Director Hiruma!
- Yes?

239
00:15:04,236 --> 00:15:07,172
Assistant Director Tange arrived by
ambulance from the detention center.

240
00:15:07,239 --> 00:15:08,107
What?

241
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:10,809
Dr. Daimon admitted him
without permission.

242
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:15,648
Nicholas Tange has
a congenital heart disease.

243
00:15:16,448 --> 00:15:18,651
Once he has an episode,
it will be too late.

244
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:29,828
- I'll take over.
- Thanks.

245
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:41,674
His heart has started again!

246
00:15:42,408 --> 00:15:43,609
He's been resuscitated.

247
00:15:44,677 --> 00:15:45,844
Inject steroids.

248
00:15:46,245 --> 00:15:48,180
- How's his blood gas?
- Here.

249
00:15:55,321 --> 00:15:56,422
He's been saved!

250
00:15:58,090 --> 00:15:59,425
Thank goodness.

251
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:14,740
Welcome back.

252
00:16:18,177 --> 00:16:20,079
Is this the hospital?

253
00:16:21,847 --> 00:16:22,982
That's right.

254
00:16:24,516 --> 00:16:28,387
Since you're at the hospital,
get fixed up before you leave.

255
00:16:30,422 --> 00:16:34,460
People die even if they're poor.

256
00:16:37,796 --> 00:16:39,064
I remembered.

257
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:43,369
I've seen you once before.

258
00:16:47,539 --> 00:16:50,242
I don't remember how many years ago
that was.

259
00:16:51,477 --> 00:16:53,979
<i>There had been an explosion</i>

260
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:56,715
<i>in a poverty-stricken neighborhood
in Brazil.</i>

261
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:02,154
Nurse!

262
00:17:02,488 --> 00:17:04,857
Miguel!

263
00:17:05,090 --> 00:17:06,392
Miguel!

264
00:17:06,592 --> 00:17:07,626
Miguel!

265
00:17:08,761 --> 00:17:09,828
Miguel!

266
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:12,064
It will be fine.

267
00:17:17,569 --> 00:17:18,804
Don't die.

268
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:22,307
Live!

269
00:17:23,008 --> 00:17:24,243
Miguel.

270
00:17:24,309 --> 00:17:30,349
<i>You tried to save children
who were beyond hope.</i>

271
00:17:31,517 --> 00:17:32,918
Live!

272
00:17:37,756 --> 00:17:39,324
So you were there.

273
00:17:39,525 --> 00:17:44,229
Just like you saved
the children back then,

274
00:17:46,298 --> 00:17:48,233
I wanted to save children

275
00:17:50,002 --> 00:17:51,870
in my own way.

276
00:17:53,172 --> 00:17:56,675
I wanted to give opportunities
to poor children.

277
00:18:01,713 --> 00:18:03,048
You still can.

278
00:18:04,116 --> 00:18:08,754
You can still give opportunities
to the children.

279
00:18:11,790 --> 00:18:14,760
If you have the surgery done
and are cured,

280
00:18:16,395 --> 00:18:18,430
you can save the future of children

281
00:18:18,530 --> 00:18:20,599
with the same congenital heart disease.

282
00:18:29,241 --> 00:18:31,810
If you're ready to die,
then surrender your life.

283
00:18:35,714 --> 00:18:37,149
For the children.

284
00:19:01,206 --> 00:19:02,441
- Director Hiruma!
- Yes?

285
00:19:02,541 --> 00:19:04,510
We heard Assistant Director Tange is
hospitalized here.

286
00:19:05,010 --> 00:19:07,212
Will he be treated at this hospital?

287
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:09,848
Will his surgery be paid for
by the people's taxes?

288
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:17,756
Well, although Nicholas Tange
has committed serious crimes,

289
00:19:17,923 --> 00:19:20,425
we are physicians,

290
00:19:21,026 --> 00:19:25,464
therefore, we will not hesitate
to save anyone's life.

291
00:19:27,399 --> 00:19:29,635
Tell us what Mr. Tange's disease is.

292
00:19:29,701 --> 00:19:32,437
I think I'll have Dr. Ushio
handle that question.

293
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,175
Allow me to answer.

294
00:19:36,909 --> 00:19:40,312
He has congenitally corrected
transposition of the great arteries.

295
00:19:40,412 --> 00:19:42,381
Can that be cured?

296
00:19:43,949 --> 00:19:46,385
There are no successful surgeries
on older people.

297
00:19:53,125 --> 00:19:54,193
I myself

298
00:19:54,927 --> 00:19:59,598
have no hesitation about saving
the life of Nicholas Tange.

299
00:20:00,899 --> 00:20:04,903
Yet, no matter how hard
talented doctors try

300
00:20:05,003 --> 00:20:07,539
to do whatever they can,

301
00:20:07,906 --> 00:20:10,008
sometimes a patient can't be saved.

302
00:20:10,842 --> 00:20:13,845
You three talented doctors

303
00:20:14,846 --> 00:20:16,315
understand that, right?

304
00:20:27,859 --> 00:20:29,461
Let me operate on Nichotan.

305
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:32,231
He'll really be in trouble
if he has another attack.

306
00:20:32,397 --> 00:20:33,465
Please.

307
00:20:36,535 --> 00:20:38,904
Would you please tell me
who this person is?

308
00:20:39,004 --> 00:20:41,073
This is no time for games!
There's no time!

309
00:20:41,173 --> 00:20:42,808
As hospital director,

310
00:20:43,342 --> 00:20:46,845
I cannot give approval for
Nicholas Tange's surgery.

311
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:50,382
Why not? You said you would save
his life at the press conference!

312
00:20:50,482 --> 00:20:52,284
I do want to save him!

313
00:20:52,451 --> 00:20:55,954
The talented doctors of
Totei University Hospital all agree

314
00:20:57,222 --> 00:20:58,624
that it is impossible!

315
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,996
Isn't that right, Dr. Ushio?

316
00:21:05,230 --> 00:21:06,465
Yes, sir.

317
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:09,668
There isn't even a surgical
procedure that can save him.

318
00:21:10,569 --> 00:21:14,006
There isn't a surgical procedure
to save him, Dr. Hamachi.

319
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:15,307
Yes, sir.

320
00:21:16,608 --> 00:21:19,544
Surgery would only hasten his death.

321
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,749
Daimon, give it up this time.

322
00:21:24,082 --> 00:21:25,450
This is the hospital's decision.

323
00:21:29,888 --> 00:21:31,623
You call yourselves doctors?

324
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:38,864
I asked if you call yourself doctors!

325
00:21:42,167 --> 00:21:44,403
Fine. I'll do it anyway.

326
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:45,604
Hey!

327
00:21:47,939 --> 00:21:49,174
Excuse me.

328
00:21:55,347 --> 00:21:58,917
Hey, Demon! You say you'll do it,
but are you actually able to?

329
00:21:59,251 --> 00:22:01,553
Nobody's ever cured a case like his.

330
00:22:04,122 --> 00:22:05,190
This is it.

331
00:22:07,225 --> 00:22:08,694
His heart ventricles are reversed.

332
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:11,296
His right atrium goes to his left
ventricle then to his pulmonary artery.

333
00:22:11,363 --> 00:22:14,299
His left atrium goes to
his right ventricle then to his aorta.

334
00:22:14,466 --> 00:22:17,536
Due to his age, we can't maintain
the blood flow to the lungs

335
00:22:17,602 --> 00:22:18,904
in the usual Fontan procedure.

336
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:21,006
Even if you physiologically
try to repair it,

337
00:22:21,073 --> 00:22:22,941
since he also has subvalvular stenosis,

338
00:22:23,041 --> 00:22:24,876
it's doubtful his left ventricle
will function.

339
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:26,945
That's right. Did you hear that?

340
00:22:27,045 --> 00:22:28,246
There's no way it can be done.

341
00:22:28,513 --> 00:22:31,950
It's possible if we divert
blood flow with a double switch.

342
00:22:32,050 --> 00:22:35,120
But it could cause stenosis
at the ventricle switch.

343
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:38,924
It's not only more complex,
it's too invasive.

344
00:22:38,990 --> 00:22:40,525
I know that!

345
00:22:40,592 --> 00:22:42,794
I'm getting gooseflesh.
We're talking like real doctors.

346
00:22:43,962 --> 00:22:46,732
Can you even perform surgery
like this on your own, Dr. Daimon?

347
00:22:46,798 --> 00:22:49,835
That's why I want you to help.

348
00:22:49,901 --> 00:22:51,403
If we do, we'll be fired.

349
00:22:51,470 --> 00:22:52,571
- Fired?
- Fired?

350
00:22:52,637 --> 00:22:54,539
Getting fired isn't anything to scoff at.

351
00:22:54,906 --> 00:22:57,175
It could end your medical career.

352
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:00,345
Are you serious about that?

353
00:23:03,482 --> 00:23:05,117
How could we possibly help you?

354
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:09,287
You made a mistake with
Kazuto's surgery the other day too!

355
00:23:10,589 --> 00:23:12,991
The flawless Michiko Daimon
no longer exists.

356
00:23:13,725 --> 00:23:15,026
So you won't do anything?

357
00:23:23,835 --> 00:23:29,040
That is the same as
watching a patient die.

358
00:23:46,625 --> 00:23:48,860
- I have a favor to ask.
- Okay.

359
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:54,399
Michiko Daimon will attempt to
perform the surgery for sure.

360
00:23:55,300 --> 00:23:57,569
I want you to prevent that.

361
00:23:57,869 --> 00:23:59,070
Yes, sir!

362
00:24:00,338 --> 00:24:02,040
- Goodbye.
- Thank you.

363
00:24:06,478 --> 00:24:07,746
- Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

364
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,682
Now that the Hiruma Fund
has been established,

365
00:24:10,916 --> 00:24:13,285
we need to speak with investors.

366
00:24:13,885 --> 00:24:16,588
Why don't we hold
a charity concert for that purpose?

367
00:24:17,355 --> 00:24:18,790
That's a good idea.

368
00:24:18,890 --> 00:24:22,661
The new Totei University Hospital
Rebirth Plan 2020 will be announced,

369
00:24:22,928 --> 00:24:24,663
and we'll gain even more investment.

370
00:24:42,581 --> 00:24:45,484
<i>There's that young pianist
who would be perfect</i>

371
00:24:45,984 --> 00:24:48,220
<i>for the charity concert.</i>

372
00:24:50,689 --> 00:24:55,994
<i>Why don't we have Kazuto Yoshiyuki
perform at the concert?</i>

373
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:58,797
But his fingers don't--

374
00:24:58,864 --> 00:25:00,232
No.

375
00:25:00,298 --> 00:25:04,402
When he tries so hard to move
his immobile fingers

376
00:25:04,603 --> 00:25:07,272
on the keyboard

377
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:09,708
and performs,

378
00:25:10,442 --> 00:25:14,179
the people will be deeply moved,
don't you think?

379
00:25:17,449 --> 00:25:18,650
Yes, sir.

380
00:25:19,551 --> 00:25:20,785
Thank you.

381
00:25:47,679 --> 00:25:50,081
What do you plan on doing, Daimon?

382
00:25:57,188 --> 00:25:58,290
It hurts.

383
00:25:59,090 --> 00:26:01,593
This is bad! Darn!

384
00:26:03,528 --> 00:26:05,163
Yes! It's ready.

385
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:07,532
It's at its most delicious now.

386
00:26:07,832 --> 00:26:08,900
Here goes.

387
00:26:14,873 --> 00:26:17,943
Kaji, it's starting to hurt.

388
00:26:23,114 --> 00:26:24,215
So...

389
00:26:24,749 --> 00:26:26,284
Just between us,

390
00:26:26,851 --> 00:26:29,854
I'm in the running for
assistant hospital director.

391
00:26:30,388 --> 00:26:31,489
- Seriously?
- Yes.

392
00:26:31,990 --> 00:26:33,725
It's between Dr. Ushio and me.

393
00:26:34,225 --> 00:26:35,927
One of us will become assistant director.

394
00:26:36,127 --> 00:26:37,362
Dr. Ushio?

395
00:26:37,529 --> 00:26:39,831
If I become assistant director,
I'll get more pay.

396
00:26:39,931 --> 00:26:42,834
If I get more pay,
I won't have to rely on life insurance

397
00:26:42,968 --> 00:26:45,303
to send my daughter to medical school.

398
00:26:45,770 --> 00:26:48,340
I want to do whatever I can
to become assistant director.

399
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,541
Hold on a second.

400
00:26:50,241 --> 00:26:51,743
What's that about life insurance?

401
00:26:54,245 --> 00:26:56,715
Dr. Ebina, may I?

402
00:26:58,984 --> 00:27:00,485
Dr. Ebina has cancer.

403
00:27:01,553 --> 00:27:02,621
Really?

404
00:27:03,488 --> 00:27:06,358
It's starting to hurt,
so I ran detailed tests.

405
00:27:06,858 --> 00:27:08,360
We're waiting for the results.

406
00:27:09,060 --> 00:27:10,061
You're kidding.

407
00:27:10,562 --> 00:27:13,131
I have something very important
to ask you.

408
00:27:13,632 --> 00:27:16,968
Could you guys perform my operation?

409
00:27:17,535 --> 00:27:18,703
- What?
- What?

410
00:27:19,104 --> 00:27:22,907
At a discount for a friend.
Daimon costs too much.

411
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:25,910
What are you talking about?
This is no time for that!

412
00:27:26,011 --> 00:27:27,245
I've also got to do

413
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:30,982
whatever it takes to prevent Daimon
from operating on Mr. Tange

414
00:27:31,216 --> 00:27:32,584
so I can become assistant director.

415
00:27:33,918 --> 00:27:35,987
That's so awful.

416
00:27:36,154 --> 00:27:37,088
What is?

417
00:27:37,155 --> 00:27:41,526
You want us to stop his surgery
but do yours instead, right?

418
00:27:44,162 --> 00:27:45,664
I need money

419
00:27:46,464 --> 00:27:47,565
for my daughter.

420
00:27:50,368 --> 00:27:52,003
I've done all I can.

421
00:27:54,706 --> 00:27:56,007
Why are you looking at me like that?

422
00:27:57,308 --> 00:27:58,476
What choice do I have?

423
00:28:01,746 --> 00:28:02,881
Darn it.

424
00:28:03,782 --> 00:28:04,983
Let's just drink.

425
00:28:05,684 --> 00:28:08,520
Master, three large draught beers.

426
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:10,522
- Certainly.
- We can't.

427
00:28:10,955 --> 00:28:12,090
Why not?

428
00:28:12,157 --> 00:28:13,391
You know why.

429
00:28:13,758 --> 00:28:15,060
We're doctors.

430
00:28:17,662 --> 00:28:18,963
Darn it.

431
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:20,131
Mamoru Hara!

432
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:22,834
I've never once gotten promoted
at someone else's expense!

433
00:28:22,901 --> 00:28:24,302
Wrong!

434
00:28:24,402 --> 00:28:27,205
You got your promotion at
the expense of...

435
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:30,909
He looks so sad. Just look at that.

436
00:28:32,110 --> 00:28:35,213
I've never seen Dr. Ebina look so pitiful.

437
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,448
You're drunk, Hara.

438
00:28:36,514 --> 00:28:38,650
Dr. Ebina, I feel

439
00:28:39,751 --> 00:28:40,952
such pity for you.

440
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:42,854
I pity you!

441
00:28:43,888 --> 00:28:45,290
Dr. Ebina!

442
00:28:45,890 --> 00:28:46,791
Dr. Ebina!

443
00:28:46,925 --> 00:28:48,226
Then you'll operate on me?

444
00:28:53,598 --> 00:28:54,799
You won't?

445
00:28:56,634 --> 00:28:59,070
Dr. Ebina, I'll do it.

446
00:28:59,170 --> 00:29:00,038
You will?

447
00:29:00,105 --> 00:29:04,075
Let's cut him open
and cut him up like crazy, Dr. Kaji!

448
00:29:04,175 --> 00:29:08,113
Nice idea! We'll slice and dice him
until he's in tiny pieces!

449
00:29:08,213 --> 00:29:09,914
Okay! Let's get to it!

450
00:29:09,981 --> 00:29:11,216
Dr. Hara, scalpel.

451
00:29:11,716 --> 00:29:14,119
That hurts. You gave it to me backwards!

452
00:29:14,619 --> 00:29:16,755
- Metzenbaum scissors!
- Metzenbaum scissors!

453
00:29:17,622 --> 00:29:20,191
One more large draught beer!

454
00:29:20,792 --> 00:29:22,227
Ready. Go!

455
00:29:25,230 --> 00:29:26,664
Oh, my goodness!

456
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:28,600
Just look at it shine!

457
00:29:28,666 --> 00:29:30,301
I haven't seen this for years!

458
00:29:30,401 --> 00:29:33,805
Pretty nice, right?
Don't say I never do nice things for you.

459
00:29:34,906 --> 00:29:36,808
What do we do? How should we cook it?

460
00:29:39,077 --> 00:29:43,081
I want shabu-shabu.
Isn't this too think for steak?

461
00:29:43,181 --> 00:29:45,116
It's too thick for shabu-shabu.

462
00:29:45,917 --> 00:29:47,919
<i>Yakiniku</i> is the best we could do?

463
00:29:47,986 --> 00:29:50,155
Yes, but it's A5 rank, so deal with it.

464
00:29:50,221 --> 00:29:52,023
Deal with it?

465
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:54,726
If you're going to complain,
then you don't get any!

466
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:55,794
- Akira!
- Fine!

467
00:29:55,860 --> 00:29:57,595
Why are you doing that?

468
00:29:57,662 --> 00:29:59,764
- No hoarding!
- Silence!

469
00:30:00,265 --> 00:30:01,566
What's that all about?

470
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:03,568
Neither of you is satisfied, right?

471
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:05,837
I mean, I wanted to have shabu-shabu.

472
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:07,405
I wanted steak.

473
00:30:07,872 --> 00:30:09,707
I'm not talking about the meat.

474
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:13,011
- Then what are you talking about?
- Nichotan's surgery.

475
00:30:14,245 --> 00:30:16,781
You haven't decided on a procedure,
have you?

476
00:30:17,649 --> 00:30:20,485
Do you have the confidence
that you'll succeed?

477
00:30:22,220 --> 00:30:25,290
But if I don't do it,
Nichotan will die for sure.

478
00:30:25,990 --> 00:30:29,527
You're not prepared.
You're flying by the seat of your pants.

479
00:30:29,594 --> 00:30:31,763
Surgery like that will never succeed!

480
00:30:32,063 --> 00:30:34,566
I worked hard to put together this agency.

481
00:30:34,799 --> 00:30:37,035
You'll ruin it for sure this time.

482
00:30:37,302 --> 00:30:41,072
So are you trying to tell me
not to perform the surgery too?

483
00:30:49,714 --> 00:30:50,849
What are those?

484
00:30:51,249 --> 00:30:53,518
Airplane tickets?

485
00:30:53,585 --> 00:30:55,587
Totei University is through.

486
00:30:55,753 --> 00:30:58,356
Michiko, I don't want you to

487
00:30:58,556 --> 00:31:02,227
fail operating at that horrible hospital.

488
00:31:03,461 --> 00:31:06,564
Why don't the three of us
go to America together?

489
00:31:06,631 --> 00:31:09,033
Here you go! Take it!

490
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,369
Here! Take it!

491
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:14,806
You can operate all you want in the US.

492
00:31:15,006 --> 00:31:16,641
Isn't that right, Michiko?

493
00:31:25,683 --> 00:31:26,751
Michiko!

494
00:31:29,220 --> 00:31:31,723
Doing nothing would be
abandoning a patient.

495
00:31:31,789 --> 00:31:32,991
I don't abandon patients.

496
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:36,127
Me neither. Gone!

497
00:31:37,061 --> 00:31:38,596
I can't believe this.

498
00:31:38,763 --> 00:31:41,799
Being around you two is
really aggravating!

499
00:31:44,903 --> 00:31:47,105
Okay. I guess I'll eat this.

500
00:31:52,844 --> 00:31:54,212
It's delicious.

501
00:31:54,879 --> 00:31:57,382
You don't want any?
Then I'll have it alone.

502
00:31:57,715 --> 00:31:59,684
We'll eat it. Here you go.

503
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:02,620
- Delicious!
- Give me one.

504
00:32:02,887 --> 00:32:03,922
Here.

505
00:32:04,489 --> 00:32:06,624
- Delicious!
- Delicious!

506
00:32:09,460 --> 00:32:13,831
<i>There is no treatment to handle
Nicholas Tange's condition.</i>

507
00:32:17,201 --> 00:32:18,436
The Rastelli procedure.

508
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:23,708
<i>The chance of a successful Rastelli
procedure on Nicholas Tange is</i>

509
00:32:23,808 --> 00:32:25,109
<i>zero percent.</i>

510
00:32:27,679 --> 00:32:31,049
Even Daimon can't perform this surgery.

511
00:32:37,388 --> 00:32:38,723
I'm putting on a mask.

512
00:32:39,490 --> 00:32:40,658
- Beta blocker too.
- Right.

513
00:32:47,765 --> 00:32:48,800
There isn't time.

514
00:32:56,007 --> 00:32:57,675
Daimon, don't do anything foolish.

515
00:32:58,042 --> 00:32:59,877
I'll stop you, no matter what you try.

516
00:33:00,044 --> 00:33:02,080
I especially won't let you
perform surgery!

517
00:33:02,180 --> 00:33:03,915
Understand? Okay?

518
00:33:05,583 --> 00:33:08,753
CHARITY CONCERT WITH KAZUTO YOSHIYUKI

519
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:17,128
- Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

520
00:33:17,195 --> 00:33:18,463
I've brought someone.

521
00:33:19,364 --> 00:33:22,967
CEO Strassberg has promised
to invest 500 million.

522
00:33:37,982 --> 00:33:41,619
Dr. Daimon,
will you give this to Dr. Ebina?

523
00:33:41,719 --> 00:33:42,754
No, I won't.

524
00:33:43,121 --> 00:33:45,556
Everyone else is at the charity concert,

525
00:33:45,623 --> 00:33:47,525
so please take care of this.

526
00:33:52,230 --> 00:33:54,065
TAKASHI EBINA
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

527
00:33:56,300 --> 00:33:58,202
TEST RESULTS

528
00:34:01,272 --> 00:34:05,643
CHARITY CONCERT WITH KAZUTO YOSHIYUKI

529
00:34:09,847 --> 00:34:13,151
Okay, give us
a moving performance, please.

530
00:34:59,464 --> 00:35:01,065
Just checking up.

531
00:35:17,448 --> 00:35:18,983
Let's samba.

532
00:35:20,318 --> 00:35:21,953
Hey, what did you just do?

533
00:35:22,019 --> 00:35:24,122
I was just checking his breathing.

534
00:35:54,785 --> 00:35:56,120
Ready to do this?

535
00:36:08,699 --> 00:36:11,202
Why isn't there any pulse?

536
00:36:16,474 --> 00:36:17,642
Out of the way.

537
00:36:19,944 --> 00:36:22,780
His cyanosis is getting worse.
Prep for emergency surgery.

538
00:36:22,880 --> 00:36:24,282
Don't you operate! Don't you dare!

539
00:36:24,682 --> 00:36:26,083
Operating room one is open.

540
00:36:26,884 --> 00:36:27,985
Take him away.

541
00:36:29,153 --> 00:36:31,389
- Don't! I told you not to!
- Oh, right.

542
00:36:32,690 --> 00:36:33,925
Your test results.

543
00:36:34,625 --> 00:36:35,860
It's benign.

544
00:36:36,727 --> 00:36:39,163
Benign? Are these my results?

545
00:36:39,997 --> 00:36:41,299
Benign?

546
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:43,801
BENIGN DISEASE

547
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:46,671
It's benign. I don't have cancer.

548
00:36:46,771 --> 00:36:50,408
I don't have cancer! This is so great!

549
00:36:56,180 --> 00:36:58,049
CHARITY CONCERT WITH KAZUTO YOSHIYUKI

550
00:37:12,797 --> 00:37:14,632
What's the matter? Isn't he feeling well?

551
00:37:46,163 --> 00:37:47,365
Let's do this, Nichotan.

552
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:49,900
Let's samba.

553
00:38:07,885 --> 00:38:09,487
What's going on here?

554
00:38:10,388 --> 00:38:12,590
He's playing with both hands
with no problem.

555
00:38:13,190 --> 00:38:14,625
This is proof of

556
00:38:14,725 --> 00:38:17,762
how advanced treatment is
at Totei University.

557
00:38:17,828 --> 00:38:18,996
It's a good thing.

558
00:38:19,463 --> 00:38:20,598
Oh, right.

559
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:22,466
Are you sure?

560
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:24,869
Dr. Daimon didn't mess up.

561
00:38:26,370 --> 00:38:30,007
Kazuto must have worked very hard
at his rehabilitation.

562
00:38:33,711 --> 00:38:35,880
Dr. Daimon knew this would happen.

563
00:38:36,113 --> 00:38:38,215
<i>All you're thinking about is the present.</i>

564
00:38:52,797 --> 00:38:54,865
- I've incised the hypodermis. Monopolar.
- Yes.

565
00:39:19,390 --> 00:39:21,425
Starting circulation at 32 degrees.

566
00:39:21,926 --> 00:39:23,461
I'll start with the atrium switch.

567
00:39:23,561 --> 00:39:26,263
What? Not the arterial switch?
That's not what you planned.

568
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:27,631
I know. This is first.

569
00:39:27,898 --> 00:39:29,700
Are you still undecided?

570
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:30,901
Incising right atrium.

571
00:39:31,168 --> 00:39:32,770
- Lower my loupe.
- Okay.

572
00:39:33,437 --> 00:39:34,438
- Metzenbaum.
- Here.

573
00:39:36,006 --> 00:39:38,008
Bring four more units of blood.

574
00:39:38,075 --> 00:39:39,343
Okay. I'll get them.

575
00:39:49,353 --> 00:39:50,721
DADDY

576
00:39:53,524 --> 00:39:55,793
CHANGE AND CHALLENGE

577
00:39:58,195 --> 00:39:59,764
If the surgery succeeds,

578
00:40:00,831 --> 00:40:02,199
I won't be assistant director.

579
00:40:02,967 --> 00:40:06,370
What will you do Ebina?
Are you a physician?

580
00:40:07,772 --> 00:40:09,006
Or are you a dog?

581
00:40:11,175 --> 00:40:13,043
Will you continue licking his boots

582
00:40:14,979 --> 00:40:16,247
and barking "woof"?

583
00:40:17,982 --> 00:40:19,250
Woof!

584
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:21,152
Go in, and I'm fired.

585
00:40:21,852 --> 00:40:23,087
Go in, and I'm fired.

586
00:40:24,722 --> 00:40:25,956
What are you doing?

587
00:40:26,023 --> 00:40:28,759
What? Well...

588
00:40:28,926 --> 00:40:31,529
Any man who hesitates
when facing death is no doctor.

589
00:40:32,797 --> 00:40:34,965
In fact, he's not even a man!

590
00:40:58,122 --> 00:40:59,323
It's from Dr. Ebina.

591
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:03,160
This is bad.

592
00:41:03,861 --> 00:41:05,629
Daimon has started operating alone.

593
00:41:06,564 --> 00:41:08,466
She can't do that operation alone.

594
00:41:08,866 --> 00:41:10,701
Don't tell me you're going.

595
00:41:12,837 --> 00:41:14,038
Dr. Kaji.

596
00:41:15,206 --> 00:41:19,009
If we help with this surgery,
we can never come back here.

597
00:41:19,910 --> 00:41:21,412
We'll be through as doctors.

598
00:41:21,879 --> 00:41:23,914
- I know that.
- No, you don't.

599
00:41:24,715 --> 00:41:27,852
Operating without patient approval
is a crime.

600
00:41:28,586 --> 00:41:30,488
If the patient died,

601
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:32,790
you'll go to prison instead.

602
00:41:36,660 --> 00:41:37,928
If talented physicians

603
00:41:38,529 --> 00:41:42,666
like us continue working,
we can save lots of patients.

604
00:41:44,101 --> 00:41:45,436
That's exactly right.

605
00:41:50,541 --> 00:41:51,876
But...

606
00:41:53,544 --> 00:41:54,979
So you won't do anything?

607
00:41:55,346 --> 00:42:00,351
That is the same as
watching a patient die.

608
00:42:03,420 --> 00:42:05,022
She's exactly right.

609
00:42:06,223 --> 00:42:08,993
When there's a life we could save
right in front of us...

610
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:11,962
Not to help him would be...

611
00:42:20,237 --> 00:42:22,006
It would weigh heavy on our conscience.

612
00:42:23,073 --> 00:42:24,241
You're right.

613
00:42:26,010 --> 00:42:27,444
Shall we go?

614
00:42:38,289 --> 00:42:40,291
It appears a rebellion has begun.

615
00:42:40,624 --> 00:42:44,828
A rebellion? Then we'll have to crush it.

616
00:43:04,848 --> 00:43:07,217
- Ebina, here to help.
- Tako, here to help.

617
00:43:07,284 --> 00:43:08,485
What took you so long?

618
00:43:08,586 --> 00:43:11,221
Ebi, you open up the view.
Tako, you suction.

619
00:43:11,322 --> 00:43:12,323
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

620
00:43:12,389 --> 00:43:14,224
- Forceps. Retractor.
- Here.

621
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:17,795
- My loupe.
- Right.

622
00:43:28,872 --> 00:43:30,641
Atrium switch complete.

623
00:43:30,808 --> 00:43:32,443
- Add myocardiac protection liquid.
- Right.

624
00:43:32,876 --> 00:43:34,745
- Incising right ventricle. Scalpel.
- Here.

625
00:43:35,913 --> 00:43:37,948
Myocardiac protection liquid
pressure climbing.

626
00:43:38,148 --> 00:43:39,149
What?

627
00:43:39,883 --> 00:43:41,785
There could be stenosis
in the coronary artery.

628
00:43:42,486 --> 00:43:44,788
If the myocardiac protection liquid
can't get in,

629
00:43:44,888 --> 00:43:47,491
we can only keep the heart stopped
for 20 more minutes. Hurry.

630
00:43:48,192 --> 00:43:50,527
First, ablate the coronary artery.

631
00:43:50,995 --> 00:43:51,996
- Metzenbaum.
- Here.

632
00:43:57,401 --> 00:44:00,270
This isn't working. We need more help.

633
00:44:05,643 --> 00:44:07,878
Thanks to you, we're all getting fired.

634
00:44:08,312 --> 00:44:09,913
Dr. Kaji!

635
00:44:10,280 --> 00:44:14,485
Now, my perfect life plan has been ruined.

636
00:44:15,886 --> 00:44:17,221
I'm sorry, Dr. Daimon.

637
00:44:17,921 --> 00:44:19,857
You didn't fail.

638
00:44:21,358 --> 00:44:23,794
That's fast! You got this far alone?

639
00:44:23,861 --> 00:44:25,596
Quit whinging.

640
00:44:25,663 --> 00:44:27,631
We need to do a coronary bypass too.

641
00:44:28,032 --> 00:44:31,168
Harvest a large saphenous vein
and trim the pericardium.

642
00:44:31,235 --> 00:44:32,202
- Right.
- Right.

643
00:44:36,473 --> 00:44:38,642
Wow! I'm getting gooseflesh again.

644
00:44:39,309 --> 00:44:41,445
What incredible teamwork!

645
00:44:50,554 --> 00:44:52,823
CHARITY CONCERT WITH KAZUTO YOSHIYUKI

646
00:45:05,569 --> 00:45:07,538
Magnificent. Bravo!

647
00:45:12,876 --> 00:45:15,245
The investors are deeply moved.

648
00:45:15,779 --> 00:45:17,481
We're sure to get enough investment.

649
00:45:17,915 --> 00:45:20,551
It's a splendid beginning to
the Hiruma Fund.

650
00:45:25,355 --> 00:45:28,759
I would like to express my thanks
to two people.

651
00:45:29,226 --> 00:45:31,762
One is Dr. Michiko Daimon.

652
00:45:32,196 --> 00:45:35,199
Since Dr. Daimon cured my disease,

653
00:45:35,566 --> 00:45:38,402
I am able to play the piano again.

654
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:41,872
Thank you, Dr. Daimon.

655
00:45:43,307 --> 00:45:45,676
The other person is Nicholas Tange.

656
00:45:46,343 --> 00:45:48,345
Without Nicholas Tange,

657
00:45:48,445 --> 00:45:50,714
I never would have started
playing the piano.

658
00:45:51,482 --> 00:45:53,784
Nicholas gave me an opportunity,

659
00:45:54,585 --> 00:45:57,221
that's why I'm here right now.

660
00:45:57,955 --> 00:46:00,491
Thank you, Nicholas.

661
00:46:03,727 --> 00:46:05,729
Michiko Daimon, bravo!

662
00:46:11,235 --> 00:46:12,436
Nicholas!

663
00:46:14,605 --> 00:46:16,240
What is that brat talking about?

664
00:46:18,809 --> 00:46:19,810
Ushio.

665
00:46:20,010 --> 00:46:21,845
- Ushio!
- Yes?

666
00:46:22,312 --> 00:46:25,215
You know what's up. Handle it.

667
00:46:55,179 --> 00:46:56,280
What's wrong, Daimon?

668
00:46:57,648 --> 00:46:58,782
It's no good.

669
00:46:59,349 --> 00:47:01,118
The subvalvular stenosis is too strong.

670
00:47:01,552 --> 00:47:02,986
What do you mean it's no good?

671
00:47:03,320 --> 00:47:04,588
What'll we do?

672
00:47:05,289 --> 00:47:06,390
Ms. Daimon?

673
00:47:10,727 --> 00:47:12,863
- Demon!
- What's wrong, Demon?

674
00:47:13,931 --> 00:47:15,465
You can do it!

675
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:25,242
<i>Resect the coronary artery button.</i>

676
00:47:25,409 --> 00:47:28,278
<i>Perform an arterial switch.</i>

677
00:47:28,879 --> 00:47:30,280
What? Ai?

678
00:47:32,082 --> 00:47:35,219
That won't remedy
the subvalvular stenosis.

679
00:47:39,890 --> 00:47:41,658
Resect the aortic valve at the base,

680
00:47:42,426 --> 00:47:44,461
move it into the new route
for the left ventricle.

681
00:47:44,561 --> 00:47:45,796
That will remedy the stenosis.

682
00:47:45,863 --> 00:47:46,864
Dr. Ushio!

683
00:47:47,798 --> 00:47:51,235
Dr. Daimon, this is the solution
you were after, right?

684
00:47:51,902 --> 00:47:53,003
Ai.

685
00:47:53,804 --> 00:47:57,941
<i>According to fluid dynamics
calculations of blood flow,</i>

686
00:47:58,108 --> 00:48:01,345
<i>circulation will be 95 percent of normal.</i>

687
00:48:01,445 --> 00:48:05,582
Dr. Ushio, when did you have the AI
deep learn this data?

688
00:48:05,749 --> 00:48:07,150
I'm a doctor, after all.

689
00:48:07,885 --> 00:48:09,486
But this is an untried procedure.

690
00:48:09,987 --> 00:48:11,321
I can't perform it.

691
00:48:12,856 --> 00:48:14,858
A complete double switch?

692
00:48:15,125 --> 00:48:17,794
But you can do it, right?

693
00:48:19,930 --> 00:48:20,964
Good idea.

694
00:48:24,201 --> 00:48:26,470
I'll start by excising
the aorta from the base.

695
00:48:28,906 --> 00:48:29,806
Here.

696
00:48:30,307 --> 00:48:32,609
You make a pericardium roll with a valve.

697
00:48:32,676 --> 00:48:34,645
- Got it.
- I'll assist.

698
00:48:34,711 --> 00:48:38,048
You two measure and prep
a heart repair patch.

699
00:48:38,115 --> 00:48:39,249
- Right.
- Got it.

700
00:48:39,449 --> 00:48:41,752
- Kin, suction, please.
- Sure.

701
00:48:42,352 --> 00:48:44,288
You expose the base.

702
00:48:46,490 --> 00:48:48,325
- Loupe.
- Okay.

703
00:49:01,538 --> 00:49:04,808
What do you want?
I won't let you interfere!

704
00:49:08,712 --> 00:49:09,846
Go ahead.

705
00:49:15,519 --> 00:49:17,854
SURGERY TIME

706
00:49:21,959 --> 00:49:24,161
Aorta base reconstruction complete.

707
00:49:24,227 --> 00:49:25,929
Next, right ventricle flow route
reconstruction.

708
00:49:25,996 --> 00:49:26,997
- Metzenbaum.
- Here.

709
00:49:33,837 --> 00:49:35,205
She's fast.

710
00:49:35,405 --> 00:49:37,507
But even at this speed...

711
00:49:37,574 --> 00:49:39,576
His heart's been stopped
for two hours and thirty minutes.

712
00:49:39,943 --> 00:49:42,212
More than three hours is dangerous.

713
00:49:42,980 --> 00:49:44,247
Will it be all right?

714
00:49:44,481 --> 00:49:46,917
You've still got
the mid-coronary anastomosis.

715
00:49:46,984 --> 00:49:47,918
Hold this.

716
00:50:01,798 --> 00:50:05,435
You can still give opportunities
to the children.

717
00:50:05,535 --> 00:50:07,838
If you have the surgery done
and are cured,

718
00:50:07,904 --> 00:50:09,906
you can save the future of children

719
00:50:10,007 --> 00:50:11,942
with the same congenital heart disease.

720
00:50:14,244 --> 00:50:16,580
If you're ready to die,
then surrender your life.

721
00:50:17,948 --> 00:50:19,483
For the children.

722
00:50:21,451 --> 00:50:22,786
Dr. Daimon.

723
00:50:24,955 --> 00:50:26,723
Perform the surgery.

724
00:50:30,761 --> 00:50:31,661
I...

725
00:50:33,363 --> 00:50:35,232
absolutely never fail.

726
00:50:50,747 --> 00:50:52,082
She's going even faster.

727
00:50:52,349 --> 00:50:53,550
Amazing.

728
00:50:59,923 --> 00:51:01,858
Repeat basic surgical moves

729
00:51:03,760 --> 00:51:05,395
until they flow like a river.

730
00:51:07,998 --> 00:51:10,267
Create a beautiful surgical field.

731
00:51:11,368 --> 00:51:14,004
That's the ideal surgery.

732
00:51:31,688 --> 00:51:34,858
And most important of all is

733
00:51:36,960 --> 00:51:38,728
no matter how tough the surgery,

734
00:51:39,563 --> 00:51:43,066
never abandon the patient.

735
00:51:58,048 --> 00:51:59,349
Nicholas...

736
00:52:19,769 --> 00:52:20,971
Heartbeat has returned.

737
00:52:22,105 --> 00:52:23,940
- Good!
- Thank goodness!

738
00:52:24,040 --> 00:52:25,475
- Daimon!
- We did it!

739
00:52:26,610 --> 00:52:27,811
Good.

740
00:52:28,211 --> 00:52:31,214
Clear out all the air. 5-0 monofilament.

741
00:52:48,231 --> 00:52:49,232
What are his vitals?

742
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:54,204
BP, 125 over 81. Pulse, 78, sinus.

743
00:52:56,606 --> 00:52:57,707
Done.

744
00:52:59,442 --> 00:53:00,544
Well done.

745
00:53:00,644 --> 00:53:02,245
- Nice work.
- Nice work.

746
00:53:02,479 --> 00:53:04,314
- Well done.
- Nice work.

747
00:53:11,388 --> 00:53:12,589
Well done.

748
00:53:14,090 --> 00:53:15,325
Everyone.

749
00:53:16,726 --> 00:53:18,028
Thank you.

750
00:53:27,170 --> 00:53:28,538
Bravo!

751
00:53:32,375 --> 00:53:33,677
OPERATING ROOM

752
00:53:46,856 --> 00:53:47,991
Michiko Daimon.

753
00:53:48,658 --> 00:53:49,859
You got

754
00:53:49,960 --> 00:53:54,531
the talented doctors of my
Totei University Hospital involved in

755
00:53:55,365 --> 00:53:59,402
a very dangerous surgery without approval.

756
00:54:00,470 --> 00:54:04,841
You used the patient, Nicholas Tange,
as a guinea pig.

757
00:54:06,910 --> 00:54:09,879
You're a disgrace to
the medical profession.

758
00:54:11,248 --> 00:54:13,483
As the hospital director,
I cannot allow this.

759
00:54:15,218 --> 00:54:18,989
You and all those who assisted you
in your operation are

760
00:54:19,289 --> 00:54:21,124
no longer doctors.

761
00:54:24,995 --> 00:54:27,197
Today, they were all doctors.

762
00:54:28,798 --> 00:54:29,966
All except you.

763
00:54:32,902 --> 00:54:35,872
Leave my Totei University Hospital

764
00:54:36,539 --> 00:54:37,540
immediately.

765
00:54:38,642 --> 00:54:40,910
Fine. You don't need to tell me.

766
00:54:41,611 --> 00:54:43,847
I'm a part-timer anyway.

767
00:54:46,716 --> 00:54:49,953
<i>It's one-of-a-kind</i>

768
00:54:50,220 --> 00:54:53,857
<i>We're unrivaled</i>

769
00:54:53,990 --> 00:54:58,194
<i>No strong wind can defeat us</i>

770
00:54:58,328 --> 00:55:02,866
<i>We keep marching forward</i>

771
00:55:07,971 --> 00:55:13,276
<i>Totei!</i>

772
00:55:15,078 --> 00:55:18,515
<i>Our school is our pride</i>

773
00:55:18,581 --> 00:55:22,452
<i>It's one-of-a-kind</i>

774
00:55:22,619 --> 00:55:26,756
<i>Totei!</i>

775
00:55:53,316 --> 00:55:55,118
Thank goodness!

776
00:56:12,535 --> 00:56:15,205
- Excuse me.
- What? Who is it?

777
00:56:20,176 --> 00:56:24,981
I would like to thank you
for employing Daimon and Jonouchi.

778
00:56:25,448 --> 00:56:26,649
This is a melon.

779
00:56:30,720 --> 00:56:32,355
This is the bill.

780
00:56:33,556 --> 00:56:35,091
Well...

781
00:56:35,191 --> 00:56:38,261
I was expecting you
to visit me pretty soon,

782
00:56:38,361 --> 00:56:40,930
but I didn't think
you would actually come.

783
00:56:40,997 --> 00:56:43,600
You fire everyone involved
in the rebellion

784
00:56:43,666 --> 00:56:45,468
and take all the credit for yourself.

785
00:56:45,702 --> 00:56:48,238
That's quite something, Director Hiruma.

786
00:56:49,072 --> 00:56:53,343
Oh, I found something.

787
00:56:59,482 --> 00:57:00,850
DIRECTOR HIRUMA'S BRAVE DECISION!

788
00:57:00,917 --> 00:57:03,853
Your photo is as fine as ever.

789
00:57:04,287 --> 00:57:05,388
Here you are.

790
00:57:07,891 --> 00:57:09,225
You saw?

791
00:57:11,227 --> 00:57:15,732
I heard that thanks to this, investment in

792
00:57:15,799 --> 00:57:19,369
the Hiruma fund is over ten billion yen.

793
00:57:23,239 --> 00:57:25,108
Now, you listen here.

794
00:57:25,208 --> 00:57:30,580
Your Michiko Daimon caused a rebellion.

795
00:57:30,980 --> 00:57:34,350
I had no choice but to dismiss
all the medical staff.

796
00:57:34,451 --> 00:57:37,520
I'm completely shorthanded.
It's a huge problem.

797
00:57:37,854 --> 00:57:42,158
In fact, I'd like to bill you for damages.

798
00:57:42,425 --> 00:57:44,461
Well, I see.

799
00:57:44,994 --> 00:57:46,362
All right.

800
00:57:46,429 --> 00:57:50,834
Then I will take this back.

801
00:57:50,900 --> 00:57:52,402
Really? Are you sure?

802
00:57:52,769 --> 00:57:55,638
However, instead...

803
00:57:56,406 --> 00:57:58,007
I have this.

804
00:57:59,642 --> 00:58:04,981
It's the bill for the surgery for
the genius pianist, Kazuto Yoshiyuki.

805
00:58:05,381 --> 00:58:08,485
I see. Is that how it's going to be?

806
00:58:09,118 --> 00:58:12,555
All right. I'll have a look at it.

807
00:58:12,622 --> 00:58:14,057
PLEASE PAY THE FOLLOWING AMOUNT

808
00:58:14,123 --> 00:58:16,125
"Fifty million yen"?

809
00:58:16,192 --> 00:58:17,260
"Fifty million yen"?

810
00:58:17,360 --> 00:58:18,528
"Fifty million yen"?

811
00:58:19,395 --> 00:58:25,568
You've added the cost of
Nicholas Tange's surgery to this.

812
00:58:25,635 --> 00:58:30,073
Are you kidding? We don't run
that kind of crooked business.

813
00:58:30,173 --> 00:58:32,208
"Crooked"? You're one to talk!

814
00:58:32,342 --> 00:58:34,077
You're definitely not one to talk.

815
00:58:34,177 --> 00:58:35,345
Excuse me.

816
00:58:35,812 --> 00:58:38,381
Director Hiruma,
this is the new medical staff.

817
00:58:38,481 --> 00:58:40,517
Oh, that's right.

818
00:58:40,583 --> 00:58:44,587
This is Professor McCartney of
Boston Harvard Medical University.

819
00:59:04,274 --> 00:59:06,409
There are so many of them.

820
00:59:06,643 --> 00:59:08,545
Translate for me later.
I didn't understand.

821
00:59:08,711 --> 00:59:09,746
Yes, sir.

822
00:59:10,079 --> 00:59:14,517
It appears Mr. Hiruma was eaten by
an invasive species.

823
00:59:14,851 --> 00:59:16,986
Heaven forbid!

824
00:59:17,220 --> 00:59:20,857
But I got it!

825
00:59:20,924 --> 00:59:22,525
Fifty million yen!

826
00:59:24,227 --> 00:59:25,428
Oh...

827
00:59:25,628 --> 00:59:27,530
Dr. Murasaki, where are you headed?

828
00:59:27,664 --> 00:59:29,766
We're going to Seattle.

829
00:59:30,433 --> 00:59:32,769
I think we're going to get married.

830
00:59:32,835 --> 00:59:34,637
- Thanks.
- Is that so?

831
00:59:35,338 --> 00:59:36,406
What?

832
00:59:37,941 --> 00:59:39,676
We're going to Aomori.

833
00:59:39,742 --> 00:59:41,844
There are no doctors in my village.

834
00:59:42,245 --> 00:59:43,313
That's right.

835
00:59:44,847 --> 00:59:46,783
- Oh, dear!
- Not in front of people.

836
00:59:46,883 --> 00:59:49,752
Two lovely couples!

837
00:59:49,852 --> 00:59:54,557
Congratulations! May you find happiness!

838
00:59:54,791 --> 00:59:57,961
See you!

839
00:59:58,428 --> 01:00:01,664
BEN CASEY

840
01:00:01,764 --> 01:00:04,434
It's nice to be so young
that you can start over.

841
01:00:04,534 --> 01:00:06,069
They could take the plunge.

842
01:00:06,169 --> 01:00:08,838
But then there are those guys.

843
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:12,208
<i>Pon.</i>

844
01:00:12,275 --> 01:00:15,044
There's that cry from Dr. Ebina again.

845
01:00:15,912 --> 01:00:18,982
How can I not cry after
getting fired from the hospital?

846
01:00:19,048 --> 01:00:20,617
How can I send my daughter to
medical school?

847
01:00:20,683 --> 01:00:22,218
I want to cry too.

848
01:00:22,719 --> 01:00:24,921
Getting kicked off university
medical staff at this age,

849
01:00:24,988 --> 01:00:26,189
what else can I do?

850
01:00:26,923 --> 01:00:28,524
Mom will be angry for sure.

851
01:00:28,791 --> 01:00:30,360
<i>- Pon.</i>
- There he goes too.

852
01:00:30,426 --> 01:00:32,562
You sure all cry a lot.

853
01:00:32,629 --> 01:00:33,863
Here it comes!

854
01:00:33,963 --> 01:00:35,298
- Here you go.
- Thank you!

855
01:00:35,398 --> 01:00:37,533
Here you go, Dr. Ushio. There.

856
01:00:37,634 --> 01:00:38,801
Looks good.

857
01:00:39,202 --> 01:00:41,871
This is the best thing to have
with Mahjong.

858
01:00:41,971 --> 01:00:45,241
By the way, what happened to
the internist, Ms. Hamachi?

859
01:00:45,642 --> 01:00:47,477
She quit the medical profession.

860
01:00:47,610 --> 01:00:50,546
Really? I wonder what she's become now.

861
01:00:50,647 --> 01:00:53,483
Ms. Hamachi said she can become
whatever she wants.

862
01:00:53,549 --> 01:00:54,584
<i>I wouldn't worry.</i>

863
01:00:54,684 --> 01:00:55,918
I guess you're right.

864
01:00:55,985 --> 01:00:58,721
I'm more worried about these guys.

865
01:00:59,088 --> 01:01:00,990
Are you sure you want to work here?

866
01:01:01,190 --> 01:01:04,761
I take a huge chunk in management fees.

867
01:01:04,861 --> 01:01:06,429
Roughly, how much is your cut?

868
01:01:07,196 --> 01:01:08,665
Is it 70-30?

869
01:01:14,303 --> 01:01:16,039
I get... You get...

870
01:01:17,340 --> 01:01:18,608
- Seriously?
- Seriously?

871
01:01:18,675 --> 01:01:19,742
Is that right?

872
01:01:20,643 --> 01:01:23,312
- That sure is greedy.
- Downright mean.

873
01:01:23,646 --> 01:01:25,715
Do you take that much from Daimon?

874
01:01:25,848 --> 01:01:29,218
I take more from her.
Do you have a problem with that?

875
01:01:29,385 --> 01:01:30,620
- Are you insane?
- Are you insane?

876
01:01:30,720 --> 01:01:32,422
- No way. I'm leaving.
- Yes, let's.

877
01:01:32,522 --> 01:01:35,858
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

878
01:01:42,965 --> 01:01:45,034
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

879
01:01:45,268 --> 01:01:49,305
<i>hates authority, and hates restrictions.</i>

880
01:01:49,739 --> 01:01:53,042
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

881
01:01:53,443 --> 01:01:54,911
<i>are her weapons.</i>

882
01:01:55,178 --> 01:01:59,115
Dr. Daimon? How is she?
Will Ms. Nomura get better?

883
01:01:59,315 --> 01:02:01,451
Will I be all right?

884
01:02:01,517 --> 01:02:03,086
You'll be fine, ma'am.

885
01:02:03,152 --> 01:02:05,755
I never fail.

886
01:02:06,122 --> 01:02:07,623
Thank goodness!

887
01:02:08,524 --> 01:02:10,326
It's not much,

888
01:02:10,393 --> 01:02:13,062
but there's something for you
under that rush mat.

889
01:02:13,162 --> 01:02:15,064
- Really? Are you sure?
- Yes.

890
01:02:15,231 --> 01:02:16,899
- Rush mat?
- That's right.

891
01:02:17,233 --> 01:02:18,768
The rush mat.

892
01:02:19,569 --> 01:02:20,803
The left one.

893
01:02:20,870 --> 01:02:22,672
- The left one.
- The left one?

894
01:02:23,706 --> 01:02:25,608
Here goes!

895
01:02:27,310 --> 01:02:29,112
Nukazuke pickles?

896
01:02:29,979 --> 01:02:31,547
Carrots make delicious...

897
01:02:42,558 --> 01:02:44,060
Money...

898
01:02:45,595 --> 01:02:50,967
I have plenty of it!

899
01:02:51,267 --> 01:02:53,703
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

900
01:02:54,170 --> 01:02:57,306
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>
